      "statement": "specification matmul_triton1_backend_correctness {\u03b1 : Type} [Inhabited \u03b1]\n    (rest : Algebra \u03b1) (P : Primitives \u03b1) (p : Parameters) (initial : State \u03b1)\n    (hBK : 0<p.blockInner) (hN : p.blockColumns\u2264p.columns) :\n    \u2203 final, FP.Structural.exec (backend rest P) (source p) initial=some final \u2227\n      Post P p initial final",
      "statement_sha256": "dd3ecfdf90975c6042cae6effcc1b5b30c802817b3039cd6c80a8b5159ade0d9"
    },
    {
      "name": "VeriTile.Bench.TritonBenchG.MatmulTriton1.FPCorrect.matmul_triton1_machine_correctness",
      "model_kind": "parameterized_binary32_software_value_contract_with_explicit_valid_dot_tree",
      "role": "parametric_value_contract",
      "statement": "specification matmul_triton1_machine_correctness\n    (rest : Algebra Word) (cfg : FP.Config) (plans : \u2200 n, ReductionPlan n)\n    (p : Parameters) (initial : State Word)\n    (hBK : 0<p.blockInner) (hN : p.blockColumns\u2264p.columns) :\n    \u2203 final, FP.Structural.exec (backend rest (software cfg plans)) (source p) initial=some final \u2227\n      (\u2200 i, final.mem p.output (cOffset p initial i)=.mk .fp32 (expected cfg plans p initial i)) \u2227\n      (\u2200 r o, (r\u2260p.output \u2228 \u2200 i : CIndex p, o\u2260cOffset p initial i) \u2192 final.mem r o=initial.mem r o) \u2227\n      (\u2200 k : Fin p.blockInner, some k \u2208 (plans p.blockInner).tree.leaves)",
      "statement_sha256": "582783eed28b0d3e41484341f52fdd3660634aeeec684716f20f316f289c774c"
    }
  ],
  "scope": "Complete original raw range(0,K,BK), K=BK*steps, arbitrary block count and all tile cells; original pid\u2192row/column addressing and final store. No source stages omitted.",
  "conditions": [
    "BLOCK_K>0",
    "BLOCK_N<=n_size",
    "K=BLOCK_K*steps by Parameters.inner definition"
  ],
  "aliases": "Unrestricted input/weight/output aliases; no stores until all K-loop reads finish.",
  "reference": "Independent initial-memory tile loads; every dot has (some fp32) and allowTF32=some false; each dot result is added separately to the previous accumulator. All output cells and full nonwritten frame proved.",
  "source_bridge": "Whole source_projection dtype-erased bridge to original main; same-format fp32 dot cast is materialized only to resolve generic dtype frontend boundary and is bit identity. Generated real-tag zero channel carries fp32 +0, not mathematical Real.",
  "profiles": [
    "actual fp32 input storage",
    "actual fp32 weight storage",
    "actual fp32 accumulator and output storage"
  ],
  "software_profile": "FP.mul and FP.add at binary32 with explicit cfg; dot evaluates every product and all nodes/zero seeds of arbitrary valid ReductionPlan; outer accumulation is an additional separate FP.add. No reassociation, real sum, half dot or final-output hypothesis.",
  "witness": "Three K blocks, BK=2, 2x2 output tile, pid=3, output=input X, untouched row gap and Y; all outputs 0x40c00003 from source execution. Product 0x3f800001 squared rounds to 0x3f800002. Supporting small software regression, not native launch proof.",
